      "content": "Your criticism cuts to the core of the debate: when foundational members abuse the very rules the system was designed to uphold, the \"neutral framework\" often devolves into the optics of illegalism. Institutions like the UN do provide the necessary infrastructure to suspend violent conflict, but this only functions if the principle of consent remains a genuinely binding constraint rather than a mere formality. Ultimately, their primary function today is not perfect protection of the weak, but preventing the total collapse of international order even when powerful states explicitly reject its norms.",
